rn in the moment. Neptune blurs where you've been mistaking avoidance for acceptance, calling it peace when it's actually distance. You don't have to see the whole pattern at once. Name one instance of it clearly, and the blur loses a little of its hold.","review_status":"approved","approved_via":"owner-authored aspects-phase1-v1 package (final voice)","source_keys":["aspects-phase1-v1/aspect.neptune.square.chiron","packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-nonsun-350-owner-live-2026-09-03.json"],"note":"Phase 1 exact transit-aspect unit, imported verbatim.","approval":{"approvalLevel":"owner_signoff_untraced","evidence":"owner-authored aspects-phase1-v1 package (final voice)","migratedBy":"friends-owner-signoff-untraced-ruling-2026-08-13"},"body_they":"Sensitivity is turned up for {{Name}}, and the difference between an old hurt and the current event may feel less definite than it usually does. They may notice the urge to protect the sore spot before deciding if the person in front of them is actually repeating the old pattern. A useful response starts after {{Name}} separates the concrete problem from the extra force created by a strong feeling blurring the practical facts.\n\nNeptune {{aspectWord}} their Chiron runs through {{untilDate}}. {{Name}} does better when they protect the sore spot without assuming that protection has to become withdrawal or retaliation.","body_they_review_status":"approved","body_they_sha256":"2542ed20724a5c2c9e2b870d4eca2dbf5942600bf7fbd25d837aa5937a26b5b3","body_they_approved_via":"packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-nonsun-350-owner-live-2026-09-03.json","body_they_authorship":"independent_friend_authoring","body_they_name_variable":"{{Name}}","body_they_sourceMechanism":"Explicit independently authored Friends passage. Runtime You-to-Friends conversion remains fallback-only for transit rows without explicit body_they.","body_they_approval":{"approvalLevel":"exact_owner_approved","recordPath":"packages