surfaced failure reads better as information than as a verdict. The Sun {{aspectWord}} your Sun until {{untilDate}} checks in on the year; smugness with a superior is the one expensive move.","review_status":"approved","approved_via":"owner-approved fast-planet refresh, chat 2026-07-28 (Sun/Mercury reviewed; Venus/Mars pre-approved 'fix later')","source_keys":["Hand, Planets in Transit","Rodden, Modern Transits","packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json"],"approval":{"approvalLevel":"owner_signoff_untraced","evidence":"owner-approved fast-planet refresh, chat 2026-07-28 (Sun/Mercury reviewed; Venus/Mars pre-approved 'fix later')","approvedAt":"2026-07-28","migratedBy":"friends-owner-signoff-untraced-ruling-2026-08-13"},"body_they":"Something {{Name}} thought was settled may come back with questions today. A plan needs proof, a decision-maker wants to know how the ambitious version will be funded, or a choice from months ago finally produces a result that cannot be ignored. Pushback can feel personal when {{Name}} believed the difficult part was already over.\n\nThe questions are useful if they expose something that still needs work. With the Sun {{aspectWord}} their Sun until {{untilDate}}, {{Name}} is better served by showing the preparation, fixing the weak point, and letting the result speak than by treating scrutiny as disrespect. A plan that survives the questions becomes easier to trust afterward.","body_they_review_status":"approved","body_they_sha256":"d98284a73b6a1749819643aed92681cc14a59b87772728d3f89c3af6f790b8dc","body_they_approved_via":"packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json","body_they_authorship":"independent_friend_authoring","body_they_name_variable":"{{Name}}","body_they_sourceMechanism":"Explicit independently authored Friends passage. Runtime You-to-Friends conversion remains fallback-only for transit rows without explicit body_they.","body_they_approval":{"approvalLevel":"e