tting because nobody will praise it can be finished without requiring a crisis first. Advice from someone with more experience may also be useful because {{Name}} is in a better position to hear the practical part of it.\n\nWith the Sun {{aspectWord}} their Saturn until {{untilDate}}, steady attention goes further than inspiration. {{Name}} does not need to make the task interesting. They need to finish it well enough that it stops taking up space on tomorrow's list.","body_they_review_status":"approved","body_they_sha256":"c55ff441a2c67c33f5a750594323a3aaf3ad74294801dc67926aab61dba3847c","body_they_approved_via":"packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json","body_they_authorship":"independent_friend_authoring","body_they_name_variable":"{{Name}}","body_they_sourceMechanism":"Explicit independently authored Friends passage. Runtime You-to-Friends conversion remains fallback-only for transit rows without explicit body_they.","body_they_approval":{"approvalLevel":"exact_owner_approved","recordPath":"packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json","payloadSha256":"c55ff441a2c67c33f5a750594323a3aaf3ad74294801dc67926aab61dba3847c","approvedAt":"2026-09-03"}},"body_you":"The backlog stops looking like an insult and starts looking like a list. It's a good window for the task nobody applauds: the forms, the corrections, the spreadsheet, and the follow-up email you've been postponing. An older or more experienced person's advice is worth actively seeking, and what gets finished tends to stay finished. The Sun {{aspectWord}} your Saturn until {{untilDate}} clears backlogs.","body_they":"The boring work may finally feel manageable to {{Name}} today. Forms, corrections, bookkeeping, follow-up, or a task that has been sitting because nobody will praise it can be finished without requiring a crisis first. Advice from someone with more experience may also be useful because {{Name}} is in a better position to hear the practical part of it.\n\nWith the Sun {{aspectWord}} their Saturn until {{untilDate}}, steady attention goes further than inspiration. {{Name}} does not need to make the task interesting. They need to finish it well enough that it stops taking up space on tomorrow's list.","positive_test":null,"intention":null,"ritual":null,"energy":null},"block_type":"fallback_article","lane":"serving","review_state":null,"evergreen":true,"evergreen_at":"2026-09-04T14:21:31.215Z","evergreen_by":"fallback-architecture-v3-2026-09-03c","facts":{"fallbackArchitectureV3":true,"packageVersion":"v3-2026-09-03c","packageContentHash":"f8d4e7273d688f2374d07439295c0177","packageKeyManifestHash":"ad3b78b91851349d48f78053cada7089","packageKeyCount":9271,"packagePartition":"core","packagePartitionContentHash":"53f6cf94236e1da0dfd5ca865889d724","packagePartitionKeyManifestHash":"9a49ed285ab09ef4f98e4c0ef7f8c2d8","packagePartitionKeyCount":7478,"distributionState":null,"releaseBatch":null,"packageBucket":"authored-content","content_role":"full_copy","review_status":"approved","positive_test":null,"readerServing":true,"stageOnly":false,"sourceSchemaVersion":null},"knowledge_ids":[],"source_snapshot":{"contentType":"authored-content","content_role":"full_copy","review_status":"approved","positive_test":null,"approved_via":"owner-approved fast-planet refresh, chat 2026-07-28 (Sun/Mercury reviewed; Venus/Mars pre-approved 'fix later')","source_keys":["Hand, Planets in Transit","Rodden, Modern Transits","packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json"],"importBatchId":"fallback-architecture-v3-2026-09-03c","sourcePackage":"tldrastro-fallback-architecture-v3","sourceFile":"authored-content","packageVersion":"v3-2026-09-03c","packageContentHash":"f8d4e7273d688f2374d07439295c0177","packageKeyManifestHash":"ad3b78b91851349d48f78053cada7089","packageKeyCount":9271,"packagePartition":"core","packagePartitionContentHash":"53f6cf94236e1da0dfd5ca865889d724","packagePartitionKeyManifest