ne way or another; choosing which part breaks is the available control.","sections":{"packageRecord":{"contentKey":"authored/transit-aspect/sun/uranus/hard","content_role":"full_copy","surface":"transit-aspect","headline":"","body_you":"Schedules flip today, the car or the printer picks its moment, someone does something abrupt, and a partner may be the restless one. The disruption eases when you plan something genuinely different yourself instead of defending the routine; jittery hours are the wrong ones for risky tasks, and a bridge burned in irritation is expensive to rebuild. The Sun {{aspectWord}} your Uranus until {{untilDate}} breaks the pattern one way or another; choosing which part breaks is the available control.","review_status":"approved","approved_via":"owner-approved fast-planet refresh, chat 2026-07-28 (Sun/Mercury reviewed; Venus/Mars pre-approved 'fix later')","source_keys":["Hand, Planets in Transit","Rodden, Modern Transits","packages/astro-knowledge/review/transit-aspect-friends-sun-proposed-v1.json"],"approval":{"approvalLevel":"owner_signoff_untraced","evidence":"owner-approved fast-planet refresh, chat 2026-07-28 (Sun/Mercury reviewed; Venus/Mars pre-approved 'fix later')","approvedAt":"2026-07-28","migratedBy":"friends-owner-signoff-untraced-ruling-2026-08-13"},"body_they":"{{Name}} may have to improvise around a day that refuses to follow the original plan. A schedule flips, a machine chooses the worst time to fail, someone acts abruptly, or a partner becomes the restless one. The disruption is irritating partly because it removes the illusion that the routine was fully under control.\n\nA small deliberate change can give the energy somewhere to go before frustration chooses the change instead. With the Sun {{aspectWord}} their Uranus until {{untilDate}}, {{Name}} benefits from staying flexible with plans and conservative with risky decisions made at the peak of irritation. Not every broken pattern needs to be rebuilt exactly as it was.","b